{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ESCALATE — deferral gate: not implementing. This is an explicit parking-lot 'idea' (tag `idea`, title '(parking lot)', description: 'deliberately NOT committed as active work yet ... Promote this to open only if there is demonstrated reader demand or drift pain'). Its acceptance criteria are conditional '(if promoted)'. Promotion is a human product decision that has not been made, and no demand/drift-pain evidence is recorded. Per repo policy I will not implement, claim, or --force an un-groomed idea.\n\nAdditionally, the scope is now partly OBSOLETE and needs regrooming before promotion:\n\n1. CONFIG-KEY INVENTORY — ALREADY DONE. Sibling work (ticket 3199, RP-04 S7.4) shipped `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` + generated `docs/config-reference.md` (and `docs/security.md`), derived from the typed config schema (`rebar._config_schema`) with a PORTABLE drift gate (test-based via tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py + test_generated_surface_markers.py; 'run under make test, no CI provider required'). The proposed files `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` (new) and `docs/config-reference.md` (new) therefore already exist. This half of the ticket is complete; the file_impact still lists it as '(if promoted)'.\n\n2. PYTHON PUBLIC-API INVENTORY — NOT built. `scripts/gen_api_reference.py` and `docs/python-api-reference.md` do not exist. But the ticket's own rationale notes the public API is 'comparatively stable and already described by docs/api-stability.md / docs/reuse-surface.md', i.e. low leverage.\n\nDecisions needed from a human before this can be promoted->open and implemented:\n- (a) Given the config-key inventory is already delivered+gated, should this ticket be narrowed to ONLY the Python public-API inventory, or closed as substantially superseded?\n- (b) Is there now demonstrated reader demand or drift pain for a generated Python-API reference that justifies promotion over the existing hand-authored docs/api-stability.md + docs/reuse-surface.md?\n- (c) If promoted: exact source of truth (public `__all__` per module? the api-stability manifest?), output format, and whether it becomes a blocking drift gate (must be portable — operation/test-linked, not tied to one CI provider).\n\nLeaving status as-is pending a human grooming decision."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787569943389060001,"uuid":"847a5210-a74f-4bde-9158-32917ff6de39"}